   "date": "2016-04-12T03:04:15Z",
   "subject": "Change point model in manual is O(n^2) but can be O(n)",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Given a vector v and two indices i and j, the sum from i to j is performed by v[i] + v[i+1] + ... + v[j-1] + v[j]. It can also be performed by precalculating the cumulative sum of v (call it cv), and then the sum from i to j is cv[j] - cv[i]. So changing the transformed parameters block of the change point model from:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">transformed parameters </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">T</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> lp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    lp </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rep_vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">log_unif</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> T</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">s </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">T</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">T</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>            lp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">s</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> lp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">s</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> poisson_log</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">D</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">],</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> if_else</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> s</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> e</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> l</span><span style=\"color:#660\">));</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>to<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">transformed parameters </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">T</span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> lp_e</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">T</span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> lp_l</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">T</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> lp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>    lp_e</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    lp_l</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">T</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        lp_e</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> lp_e</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> poisson_log</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">D</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">],</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> e</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        lp_l</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> lp_l</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> poisson_log</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">D</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">],</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> l</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>    lp </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rep_vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">log_unif </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> lp_l</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">T </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">],</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> T</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> head</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lp_e</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> T</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> head</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lp_l</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> T</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>results in a dramatic speed up. On my machine 10k samples of the original took 8m53s and the new one took 33s.<br><br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "mJHztR3lAgAJ",
   "from": "Bob Carpenter",
   "author": "8aa9b8cc06fdc99c",
   "date": "2016-04-12T05:09:02Z",
   "subject": "Re: [stan-users] Change point model in manual is O(n^2) but can be O(n)",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Cool!  Or should I say D&#39;Oh!?  I spent 20+ years before\r<br>Stan working on dynamic programming algorithms for natural\r<br>language processing and speech recognition!\r<br>\r<br>You can avoid saving lp_e and lp_l by making them local\r<br>variables:\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "\r<br>  transformed parameters {\r<br>    vector[T] lp;\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "    {\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "      vector[T+1] lp_e;\r<br>      vector[T+1] lp_l;\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "      lp_e[1] &lt;- 0;\r<br>      lp_l[1] &lt;- 0;\r<br>      for (t in 1:T) {\r<br>        lp_e[t + 1] &lt;- lp_e[t] + poisson_log(D[t], e);\r<br>        lp_l[t + 1] &lt;- lp_l[t] + poisson_log(D[t], l);\r<br>      }\r<br>      lp &lt;- rep_vector(log_unif + lp_l[T + 1], T) + head(lp_e, T) - head(lp_l, T);\r<br>    }\r<br>  }\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "At first it looked wrong because both probs were collected\r<br>the same way, then I noticed lp_l[T+1] in the rep_vector\r<br>and the the subtraction, which is a slick way to calculate the\r<br>same value.  (A few operations could still be saved at the edges\r<br>like the assignments to 0 and the corresponding additions, but\r<br>not worth it for the extra complication --- the way you wrote it\r<br>is very clean once you see the subtraction.)\r<br>\r<br>I&#39;ll put the new version in the manual with a bit of description\r<br>and attribute the improved version to you:\r<br>\r<br><a href=\"https://github.com/stan-dev/stan/issues/1709#issuecomment-208706085\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/stan-dev/stan/issues/1709%23issuecomment-208706085&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792461845243000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3Q_mtF6310NDTNH2h0xBf-\">https://github.com/stan-dev/stan/issues/1709#issuecomment-208706085</a>\r<br>\r<br>Thanks!\r<br>\r<br>- Bob\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "\r<br>&gt; On Apr 11, 2016, at 11:04 PM, Luke &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">lwik...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Given a vector v and two indices i and j, the sum from i to j is performed by v[i] + v[i+1] + ... + v[j-1] + v[j]. It can also be performed by precalculating the cumulative sum of v (call it cv), and then the sum from i to j is cv[j] - cv[i]. So changing the transformed parameters block of the change point model from:\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; transformed parameters {\r<br>&gt;     vector[T] lp;\r<br>&gt;     lp &lt;- rep_vector(log_unif, T);\r<br>&gt;     for (s in 1:T) {\r<br>&gt;         for (t in 1:T) {\r<br>&gt;             lp[s] &lt;- lp[s] + poisson_log(D[t], if_else(t &lt; s, e, l));\r<br>&gt;         }\r<br>&gt;     }\r<br>&gt; }\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; to\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; transformed parameters {\r<br>&gt;     vector[T+1] lp_e;\r<br>&gt;     vector[T+1] lp_l;\r<br>&gt;     vector[T] lp;\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt;     lp_e[1] &lt;- 0;\r<br>&gt;     lp_l[1] &lt;- 0;\r<br>&gt;     for (t in 1:T) {\r<br>&gt;         lp_e[t + 1] &lt;- lp_e[t] + poisson_log(D[t], e);\r<br>&gt;         lp_l[t + 1] &lt;- lp_l[t] + poisson_log(D[t], l);\r<br>&gt;     }\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt;     lp &lt;- rep_vector(log_unif + lp_l[T + 1], T) + head(lp_e, T) - head(lp_l, T);\r<br>&gt; }\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; results in a dramatic speed up. On my machine 10k samples of the original took 8m53s and the new one took 33s.\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "&gt; -- \r<br>&gt; You received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;Stan users mailing list&quot; group.\r<br>&gt; To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">stan-users+...@googlegroups.com</a>.\r<br>&gt; To post to this group, send email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">stan-...@googlegroups.com</a>.\r<br>&gt; For more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792461845243000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2hLyrXWB-SgTZdw9uw4fXK\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.\r<br>\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
